---
import SectionHeading from "../shared/SectionHeading.astro";
import { whoItsForPoints } from "../../data/home";
---

<section class="border-t border-slate-100 bg-stone-50">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-20 md:py-28">
    <SectionHeading
      eyebrow="Is This a Fit?"
      headline="Built for businesses that have outgrown fragmented marketing."
      subhead="You don't need more marketing activity. You need what you already have working together."
    />
    <p class="mt-8 max-w-3xl text-lg text-slate-600">
      EverJourneys works best with established, owner-led businesses that already
      have a proven offer and existing customers — but whose marketing,
      experience, and systems have become fragmented, inconsistent, or hard to
      predict.
    </p>
    <ul class="mt-8 max-w-2xl space-y-3">
      {
        whoItsForPoints.map((point) => (
          <li class="flex gap-3 text-slate-700">
            <span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-teal-700" />
            <span>{point}</span>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-8 max-w-3xl text-lg text-slate-600">
      The strongest fit is a business that's curious, open to testing and
      iteration, and interested in understanding why something is happening — not
      just what to do next. If you're looking for a partner to figure this out
      with, rather than a vendor to hand a list of tasks to, that's how
      EverJourneys works.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
